  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="updated">Last updated: August 2026</p>
  <p>Study Buddy ("we," "our," or "the app") is a free, student-built study tool that runs entirely in your web browser. This policy explains what information the app uses, how it is handled, and your choices. We designed Study Buddy to collect as little as possible.</p>

  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <div class="card">
    <ul>
      <li>We do <strong>not</strong> have a server that stores your data, and we do <strong>not</strong> sell or share your information.</li>
      <li>Your study data (flashcards, goals, schedule, progress, etc.) is saved <strong>only in your own browser</strong> on your device.</li>
      <li>Google Classroom data is <strong>read-only</strong>, shown to you in the app, and never stored by us or sent anywhere else.</li>
      <li>AI features are optional and only work if <strong>you</strong> add your own API key.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>Information the app uses</h2>
  <p><strong>Study data you create.</strong> When you make flashcards, set goals, build a schedule, take practice tests, or track assignments, that information is stored locally in your browser using <em>localStorage</em>. It stays on your device and is not transmitted to us. Clearing your browser data or using the app's "Erase all data" button removes it.</p>

  <p><strong>Google Classroom data (only if you connect it).</strong> If you choose to connect Google Classroom, you sign in through Google and grant read-only permission. The app then requests your class list and coursework (assignment titles, descriptions, and due dates) using Google's official Classroom API, and displays them to you. This information is used only to show you your assignments and to help you study them. It is <strong>not</strong> saved on any server, is <strong>not</strong> shared with anyone, and is only held temporarily in your browser during your session. You can disconnect at any time by revoking access in your <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Account permissions</a>.</p>

  <p><strong>AI features (optional).</strong> If you add your own third-party API key (such as Google Gemini, OpenAI, or Anthropic) in Settings, the text you send to AI features — like a question or the text of an assignment — is sent directly from your browser to that provider to generate a response. Your API key is stored only in your browser. Your use of those services is governed by that provider's own privacy policy.</p>

  <h2>Google user data &amp; Limited Use</h2>
  <div class="note">
    Study Buddy's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs to any other app will adhere to the
    <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
    including the Limited Use requirements. We only request read-only access, use the data solely to display and help you study your own assignments, do not transfer it to others, and do not use it for advertising.
  </div>

  <h2>What we do not do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We do not sell, rent, or share your personal information.</li>
    <li>We do not show ads or use your data for advertising.</li>
    <li>We do not store your Google Classroom data on any server.</li>
    <li>We do not track you across other websites.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Data security</h2>
  <p>Because your data stays in your own browser and connections to Google and AI providers use secure HTTPS, there is no central database of user information for someone to breach. Please keep your own device and accounts secure, and don't share your API keys.</p>

  <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
  <p>Study Buddy is an educational tool intended for students. It does not knowingly collect personal information on a server. If you are under 13, please use the app with a parent, guardian, or teacher's permission.</p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>We may update this policy as the app changes. The "Last updated" date at the top shows the most recent version.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>If you have questions about this policy, contact us at: <strong><a href="mailto:studybuddy.focusmode@gmail.com">studybuddy.focusmode@gmail.com</a></strong></p>

  <footer>Study Buddy — a student project. Your studying, kept private.</footer>
